## Why This Is Asked
Explores a new angle on LLM-ops: enforcing per-tenant privacy at the gateway with dynamic redaction policies, balancing data minimization with latency.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant redaction policy (strict/moderate/none)
- In-flight prompt redaction and post-processing of outputs
- Lightweight in-memory policy engine and fast lookups
- Privacy-preserving auditing and zero-PII logs

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPrompt(prompt, policy) {
  if (policy === 'strict') {
    return prompt
      .replace(/\b(\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4})\b/g, 'REDACTED_SSN')
      .replace(/\b\d{16}\b/g, 'REDACTED_CARD');
  }
  if (policy === 'moderate') {
    return prompt.replace(/email:\s*\S+@\S+/g, 'email=REDACTED');
  }
  return prompt;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify policy drift and retroactive redactions across model updates?
- What metrics and logs would you keep to demonstrate compliance without leaking data?
